{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced","id":1177913,"title":"What if a Werewolf is embraced?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-21T12:30:27-08:00","id":1177913,"title":"What if a Werewolf is embraced?","content":"I'm totally new to COfD, and while I know of abominations in the cWOD, I don't know if there are rules for a thing like an abomination in COfD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T12:56:36-08:00","id":1177921,"title":"","content":"By default, Major templates don't stack. The werewolf would be dead.<br /> <br /> That said, the Chronicles of Darkness are full of unknown magics and strange creatures and strange hybrids may be possible (mostly as NPCs). The Strix Synthesis ability is explicitly an avenue for this in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T13:34:26-08:00","id":1177928,"title":"","content":"What Maina said. There is no standard template for a mixture between a werewolf and a vampire, and at least as of first edition, the default assumption is the werewolf dies when you drain all the blood from her, but the Embrace doesn't take when you fill it with your vitae, and you're just left with a corpse. The nWoD/CofD is filled with exception cases and strange mysteries, so never say never, but any &quot;crossbreed&quot; is probably going to be the unique result of extraordinary circumstances, and would probably be some homebrew entity with more particular traits than simply stacking one template on top of the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T14:09:44-08:00","id":1177939,"title":"","content":"The ban on template stacking hasn't been reintroduced in 2E, and Dev comments in the Changeling Kickstarter have clarified that this is intentional - there's no longer a 'rule' against it.<br /> If it makes a good story, go for it.<br /> <br /> In the interest of having a good discussion, we should probably not force 'the werewolf would die' on OP as it's no longer necessarily accurate and also the most boring option.<br /> <br /> OP, I would look at the Admonitoria, which is unofficial content by a former OPP writer about a mixed Changeling/Vampire splat for inspiration. Alternatively, if it works better for you, the werewolf would die, or just become a vampire with an appropriately strange Bloodline.<br /> <br /> Editing in the full quote so that my own interpretations of intent don't throw people off:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The template stacking rules in 1e were designed to prevent players from creating Vampire/Werewolf/Mage monstrosities and becoming &quot;too powerful.&quot; When we did Vampire 2e nine years later, it became clear that was not the problem it had seemed to be at the beginning, and that trying to solve it the way we had had created another problem: that players thought &quot;major/minor template&quot; was an in-setting thing, that vampires and mages had something metaphysical in common and that ghouls and wolf-blooded had something _different_ in common.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That's not the case. Vampires and mages are two entirely different phenomena, with no magical traits in common from an in-character perspective. Vampires and werewolves... well, they share a few things, but that's mainly by virtue of both being predators. The real common trait of monsters in the Chronicles of Darkness is that they either begin as or become human. Nothing more, nothing less.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So in the 2e games, templates are strictly a mechanical convenience. We still don't recommend mixing monster types, and do it only rarely ourselves... but on a setting level, it's quite possible some beings could cross categories. And if that works for your individual chronicle, go ahead and do it.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-21-2018, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T14:37:48-08:00","id":1177942,"title":"","content":"Chiming on the \u201cIt\u2019s possible, but expect more than just Power A + Power B\u201d crowd here. <br /> <br /> The last time vampires and mages tried to \u201ccross over\u201d in canon material, we got the Tremere Liches. They aren\u2019t certainly Kindred, and while closer to the Awakened, as of 2E it seems they are neither your average \u201cmage with a few quirks.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T14:49:22-08:00","id":1177944,"title":"","content":"&quot;The individual in question wakes up as a very confused Gangrel to the delight of Ordo Dracul researchers everywhere&quot; would be the easy route. Imagine the surprise if the sire was a Daeva!<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, embracing a werewolf would probably require a handwavy in-universe explanation, as well as a fair amount of cherry picking and combining various parts of the two templates. I'd definitely rule against stacking both templates if the character is a PC. If not, the sky's the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23744-malkav-s-weird-cousin","name":"Malkav's Weird Cousin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T15:15:15-08:00","id":1177950,"title":"","content":"I think the hardest part of embracing a werewolf is killing the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T15:28:46-08:00","id":1177954,"title":"","content":"Could be a new clan, whose clan bane is chronic excruciating pain as the healing rate of the werewolf interacts with the Curse to constantly attempt to heal death. Discipline set would be a physical one reflecting the Werewolf's moon aspect, Animalism, and a strange discipline that interacts with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T17:23:55-08:00","id":1177968,"title":"","content":"Great take on it! Using silver as their Bane would be a no-brainer but I like that twist of using the former regeneration as a curse. Creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T18:17:53-08:00","id":1177977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1177954#post1177954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be a new clan, whose clan bane is chronic excruciating pain as the healing rate of the werewolf interacts with the Curse to constantly attempt to heal death. Discipline set would be a physical one reflecting the Werewolf's moon aspect, Animalism, and a strange discipline that interacts with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creepy in just the way I like it. Especially how werewolf regeneration itself can be a subject of body horror, in light of the Five Pounds of Meat thread in the Werewolf forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T19:23:16-08:00","id":1177984,"title":"","content":"There already exists a canon bloodline that is based on werewolves; Dead Wolves in the book Shadows of Mexico. The origin is only presented as a rumour, though.<br /> <br /> I also did a homebrew thing for embracing werewolves <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=1164915\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T21:32:06-08:00","id":1177994,"title":"","content":"I'd personally handle it in a manner more like the Tremere Liches than as a true blending: pick one (werewolf or vampire) and then use the tools from that gameline to push the resulting character as close to the other gameline as possible. The reasons for this are largely mechanical: you avoid the messiness of having to resolve questions such as \u201cBlood Potency, Primal Urge, or both?\u201d or \u201cHumanity or Harmony?\u201d If it's a feral vampire, it's Blood Potency and Humanity; if it's a death-touched werewolf, it's Primal Urge and Harmony. <br /> <br /> This is especially true in 2e, where each gameline has its own \u201cthematic trait mechanics\u201d (Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, Pilgrimage, Clarity, Cover, etc.) sometimes wildly different from each other and often quite elaborate. For the sake of the gamers' sanity, you don't want to double up on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T00:12:33-08:00","id":1178007,"title":"","content":"In 2E rules there is <b>official</b> way for half-werewolves, half-vampires - Embracing Wolf-Blooded. Wolf-Blooded are 'lesser' werewolves, with only few 'wolfish' powers, called Tell. Tells are <i>staying</i> with character after change into other monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's all in the <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook. Right now, in my Werewolf game I have Ordo Dracul Daeva vampire that was Wolf-Blooded before, sister to one of PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-22-2018, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T03:57:33-08:00","id":1178025,"title":"","content":"Well, some Wolf-blooded have Tells that would make them qualify for a definition of werewolf (note the lower case), other Tells are weird spiritual phenomena that are of no interest to this particular case. The one that turns you into Urshul on full moons is probably the best, followed by the ones that makes you go Dalu when angered or exposed to religious symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T06:18:41-08:00","id":1178056,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the things that simplifies the situation for 2e is the understanding that once a werewolf dies, it returns to human form. Sure, it might still be half-spirit, but that human lump there could be embraced.<br /> <br /> Now as to the side effects? You might look at just handing the character Coil of Zirnitra powers and stack up some supernatural merits. Wolf-blooded explicitly carry their supernatural Tell merit forward when they convert to another type, so you could just handwave it. A custom bloodline is feasible of course, and using regeneration and shape-shifting as a curse alongside silver sounds fantastic! <br /> <br /> One question you might answer for yourself, however would be: is this a normal thing--this embrace of a werewolf? Or is it something that doesn't happen normally but special circumstances apply? Remember as well that there are rage triggers that would have to be passed for the werewolf to lose all blood and die without, oh, going garou and ripping the vamp to shreds--even if he actually *wanted* the embrace!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:27:28-08:00","id":1178123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1177954#post1177954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be a new clan, whose clan bane is chronic excruciating pain as the healing rate of the werewolf interacts with the Curse to constantly attempt to heal death. Discipline set would be a physical one reflecting the Werewolf's moon aspect, Animalism, and a strange discipline that interacts with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea! I like the regeneration as a bane - perhaps it could manifest as an inhuman appearance too, as the regeneration (with a memory of shapeshifting) forces the body into weird proportions. For the physical one, I think I would go with Vigor or Celerity - Resilience seems at odds with using regeneration as the basis for a bane. There is a Discipline for interacting with spirits in the 1st ed book Book of the Spirit, which could be adapted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1178056#post1178056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one of the things that simplifies the situation for 2e is the understanding that once a werewolf dies, it returns to human form. Sure, it might still be half-spirit, but that human lump there could be embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting that together with Wyrdhamster's point about Wolf-Blooded, perhaps most of the werewolf template is eliminated in favour of a couple of wolf-blooded Tells.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T13:47:58-08:00","id":1178180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1178123#post1178123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting that together with Wyrdhamster's point about Wolf-Blooded, perhaps most of the werewolf template is eliminated in favour of a couple of wolf-blooded Tells.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That could be feasible. You'd want to find something to do with any XP-purchased werewolf powers. Possibly converting them into additional Tells (there's a supernatural Merit for that), or &quot;buying&quot; Protean up and giving thereby the ability to shapeshift. Protean 4 can even approximate the nastier forms to some extent, and you could custom-up some additional supernatural merits to fill in the blanks (such as increased size).<br /> <br /> A brand-new werewolf subjected to an embrace probably wouldn't get so extensive a special treatment, however. <br /> <br /> This is a fun mental exercise, as I might use the premise, myself.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:39:10-08:00","id":1178736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1178180#post1178180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be feasible. You'd want to find something to do with any XP-purchased werewolf powers. Possibly converting them into additional Tells (there's a supernatural Merit for that), or &quot;buying&quot; Protean up and giving thereby the ability to shapeshift. Protean 4 can even approximate the nastier forms to some extent, and you could custom-up some additional supernatural merits to fill in the blanks (such as increased size).<br /> <br /> A brand-new werewolf subjected to an embrace probably wouldn't get so extensive a special treatment, however. <br /> <br /> This is a fun mental exercise, as I might use the premise, myself.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>To drive home the &quot;natural&quot; shapeshifting, you could even give Protean a Vitae discount to encourage its use.<br /> <br /> Oh, another idea for a Bane is to draw on the typical Werewolf fears and the fact they get Essence from eating humans and wolves (and werewolves. And Spirits...) to make it about Hunger. Either penalties to Frenzy, needing a (scaled to Humanity) minimum amount of Vitae or risk hunger Frenzy, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-24-2018, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:40:30-08:00","id":1178920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177913-what-if-a-werewolf-is-embraced?p=1178736#post1178736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To drive home the &quot;natural&quot; shapeshifting, you could even give Protean a Vitae discount to encourage its use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae discount for Protean, but limit its application to keep it balanced? Something like &quot;Sure, you can gain some animal traits for no Vitae at all. Can a wolf crawl up walls? No? Well...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23744-malkav-s-weird-cousin","name":"Malkav's Weird Cousin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}